// ADR-0002: no `replace` directive is ever checked in. This workspace is what
// gives local development the sibling-on-disk resolution instead, and flipping
// GOWORK=off exercises the resolution a real consumer gets.
//
// The floor is go 1.26 (spelled 1.26.0, which is what golang.org/x/sys now
// requires and what excludes only the 1.26 release candidates), and it stays
// there now that Go 1.27 has shipped:
// ADR-0001 raised it to 1.27 for encoding/json/v2 alone, and ferry imports
// neither json/v2 nor jsontext, so the reason was never spent. errors.AsType
// is what holds it as high as 1.26. No file in this repository carries a
// `toolchain` directive; a consumer resolves the floor with whatever toolchain
// they have, and CI builds on both the floor and the newest released Go.
go 1.26.0

use (
	.
	./driver/env
	./driver/http
	./driver/kv
	./driver/windows
	./driver/yaml
	./examples
)
